  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Virginia has received $1.6B in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Award activity in Virginia includes 6,501 awards with an average award size of $252K. Obligations fell 98.6% year over year. Fiscal-year totals prior to FY2027 show much larger annual obligations: FY22 was $89.4B, FY23 was $106B, FY24 was $110B, FY25 was $121B, and FY26 was $119B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in Virginia for FY2027 to date, obligating $1.3B. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP is the largest vendor for FY2027 to date with $900M in obligations. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the top industry by obligation for FY2027 to date at $900M. Computer Systems Design Services and Other Computer Related Services follow with $252M and $238M respectively. The FY2027 to date snapshot is a partial fiscal-year view, and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). This summary focuses on obligations, buyer concentration, vendor concentration, and the industries that captured the largest shares of FY2027 to date obligations in Virginia.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations are $1.6B, compared with FY26 obligations of $119B. Obligations fell 98.6% year over year. Prior full fiscal years show a progression from $89.4B in FY22 to $121B in FY25 before dipping to $119B in FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal contracting in Virginia right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buying agency for FY2027 to date with $1.3B in obligations. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP is the top vendor for FY2027 to date with $900M in obligations. Computer Systems Design Services and Other Computer Related Services are the next-largest industries with $252M and $238M in obligations respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
